00:16:14,140 --> 00:16:18,020
That was all part of your
plan, wasn't it? Right again.

268
00:16:18,400 --> 00:16:20,106
You're alive for two reasons.

269
00:16:20,380 --> 00:16:23,477
First, so you could tell your
story of the failed assassination,

270
00:16:23,560 --> 00:16:27,097
placing a member of the Straw Hat
crew at the scene of the crime.

271
00:16:27,180 --> 00:16:30,780
Secondly, we were trying to
ferret out an important document.

272
00:16:31,220 --> 00:16:33,420
The blueprints of a certain ship.

273
00:16:33,980 --> 00:16:37,397
One that has been passed
down in secret from

274
00:16:37,480 --> 00:16:40,620
shipwright to chosen
apprentice for generations.

275
00:16:41,200 --> 00:16:44,080
We knew that with your
life clearly in danger,

276
00:16:44,260 --> 00:16:48,436
you would pass that document on to
someone you trusted to keep it safe.

277
00:16:48,640 --> 00:16:51,060
You made that choice earlier tonight.

278
00:16:51,320 --> 00:16:53,160
Your foreman, Paulie.

279
00:16:54,420 --> 00:16:57,077
Our associates are with
him this very moment.

280
00:16:57,160 --> 00:17:00,677
It's all going as planned, isn't it?

281
00:17:00,760 --> 00:17:03,517
You must be very damn proud of yourself.

282
00:17:03,600 --> 00:17:07,757
I want you to see this to its end.

283
00:17:07,840 --> 00:17:12,777
Of course, I'll go deal with the
riffraff standing guard outside the door.

284
00:17:12,860 --> 00:17:17,817
When the blueprints are secured, our
associates will contact you at that time.

285
00:17:17,900 --> 00:17:20,917
You will have full clearance
to dispose of iceberg.

286
00:17:21,000 --> 00:17:22,600
Do so at once.

287
00:17:25,060 --> 00:17:27,400
Make sure he dies without fail.

288
00:17:28,220 --> 00:17:31,817
After that, the only remaining
loose end will be Polly.

289
00:17:31,900 --> 00:17:36,057
He dies, and the truth of what's
happened here dies with him.

290
00:17:36,140 --> 00:17:40,260
The blame will remain on the Straw
Hats, and no one's the wiser.

291
00:17:43,840 --> 00:17:45,857
I know he doesn't listen to me.

292
00:17:45,940 --> 00:17:49,177
It's crazy, but I thought maybe
he'd listen to his own advice.

293
00:17:49,260 --> 00:17:51,300
We are talking about Luffy.

294
00:17:52,380 --> 00:17:53,210
Hey, guys,

295
00:17:53,293 --> 00:17:56,777
do you think that's Robin in the middle
of all that commotion down at Galley Law?

296
00:17:56,860 --> 00:18:00,297
No matter what Luffy decided to
do, we still gotta be careful.

297
00:18:00,380 --> 00:18:01,210
Yeah, I know.

298
00:18:01,300 --> 00:18:04,947
But him rushing in like that
might actually work in our favor.

299
00:18:05,240 --> 00:18:07,277
If you think about the way he does things,

300
00:18:07,360 --> 00:18:10,917
is he the kind of guy that's gonna go
in through the back or side entrance?

301
00:18:11,000 --> 00:18:13,217
Not his style. No way. So,

302
00:18:13,300 --> 00:18:16,817
I'm pretty sure by now he's made a go at
barging straight through the front door.

303
00:18:16,900 --> 00:18:19,377
And it's safe to assume that
right now he's running around

304
00:18:19,460 --> 00:18:22,197
inside like crazy because he
has no idea where he's going,

305
00:18:22,280 --> 00:18:23,110
don't you think?

306
00:18:23,193 --> 00:18:24,023
Oh, yeah.

307
00:18:24,106 --> 00:18:24,940
Sounds like him.

308
00:18:25,580 --> 00:18:26,410
Uh-huh.

309
00:18:26,493 --> 00:18:27,917
And from the shipwright's point of view,

310
00:18:28,000 --> 00:18:30,157
he's the leader of the
group that attacked Iceberg.

311
00:18:30,240 --> 00:18:31,957
So if you made it in there by now,

312
00:18:32,040 --> 00:18:34,617
all of those guys are going to
be busy trying to catch him.

313
00:18:34,700 --> 00:18:37,797
Which would mean the guards have
severely thinned out at the front door.

314
00:18:37,880 --> 00:18:40,177
Or at the very least, they're
completely distracted.

315
00:18:40,260 --> 00:18:42,737
So the safest way in right
now is through the front,

316
00:18:42,820 --> 00:18:45,157
right behind all the
chaos in Luffy's wake.

317
00:18:45,240 --> 00:18:47,237
So when he does it,
it's completely stupid.

318
00:18:47,320 --> 00:18:50,177
But if we do the same exact thing,
it's actually a brilliant plan, huh?

319
00:18:50,260 --> 00:18:51,320
Yeah, makes sense.

320
00:18:51,540 --> 00:18:53,716
I say that we should go for it, then.

321
00:18:53,920 --> 00:18:55,508
The gate is right up ahead.

322
00:18:55,820 --> 00:18:57,080
Okay, ready?

323
00:18:58,360 --> 00:18:59,480
It's showtime!

324
00:18:59,700 --> 00:19:00,780
Here we go!

325
00:19:14,660 --> 00:19:16,940
This was a dumb idea!

326
00:19:18,540 --> 00:19:20,500
Crap, this sucks.

327
00:19:20,920 --> 00:19:24,600
I wanted to jump right through
the front door like a typhoon.

328
00:19:25,700 --> 00:19:28,440
But I'm totally stuck.

329
00:19:32,140 --> 00:19:34,840
But I'm totally stuck.

330
00:19:35,560 --> 00:19:37,360
Gotta get out.

331
00:19:37,760 --> 00:19:40,260
Gotta get Robin.

332
00:19:56,880 --> 00:19:59,380
Oh, what the hell is going on?

333
00:20:02,800 --> 00:20:05,120
We need help on the third floor!

334
00:20:05,380 --> 00:20:07,177
Somebody come to the presence room quick!

335
00:20:07,260 --> 00:20:08,357
The guards are wiped out!

336
00:20:08,440 --> 00:20:09,300
I need backup!

337
00:20:09,800 --> 00:20:11,500
What do you mean wiped out?

338
00:20:12,900 --> 00:20:13,730
Tilestone!

339
00:20:13,813 --> 00:20:15,617
Kokoro and Luchi should be there!

340
00:20:15,700 --> 00:20:16,720
Well, come see!

341
00:20:16,940 --> 00:20:18,040
What?

342
00:20:29,600 --> 00:20:30,430
What?

343
00:20:30,760 --> 00:20:31,720
No way!

344
00:20:32,140 --> 00:20:33,320
Still no word.

345
00:20:33,560 --> 00:20:36,560
I'm getting tired of dealing
with all these idiots.

346
00:20:36,720 --> 00:20:38,460
How dare you!

347
00:20:38,980 --> 00:20:40,980
I'll kill you, bastard!

348
00:20:42,720 --> 00:20:44,317
You're a noisy one, aren't you?

349
00:20:44,400 --> 00:20:46,760
If you lay a single finger on Mr.

350
00:20:46,920 --> 00:20:49,137
Iceberg, I'll tear you limb from limb!

351
00:20:49,220 --> 00:20:51,357
I'd like to see you try...

352
00:20:51,440 --> 00:20:52,740
Iron Body.

353
00:21:07,180 --> 00:21:08,920
Push that giant hammer!

354
00:21:09,180 --> 00:21:10,240
That's not good.

355
00:21:12,560 --> 00:21:13,390
You!

356
00:21:13,473 --> 00:21:15,957
Get your hands off me! Hmph.

357
00:21:16,040 --> 00:21:17,922
Are those muscles just for show?

358
00:21:18,080 --> 00:21:19,540
I can't move my arm!

359
00:21:19,860 --> 00:21:21,801
How is this guy stronger than me?

360
00:21:38,500 --> 00:21:42,680
Oh, he's taken out three
foremen, all on his own.

361
00:21:48,580 --> 00:21:51,340
Peak Rain Force must not stand! Shave.

362
00:21:57,860 --> 00:21:59,020
We found them!

363
00:21:59,140 --> 00:22:00,669
It's Roro, Noah, and Zoro!

364
00:22:00,860 --> 00:22:02,037
They finally showed up!

365
00:22:02,120 --> 00:22:03,497
Don't let them get away!

366
00:22:03,580 --> 00:22:05,345
That woman is one of them two!

367
00:22:06,260 --> 00:22:08,560
If Luffy isn't here, then where is he?

368
00:22:08,720 --> 00:22:10,838
I don't know, why are you asking me?

369
00:22:12,940 --> 00:22:13,770
What now?

370
00:22:14,400 --> 00:22:17,717
Well, they've already found us, so
there's no point in trying to be sneaky.

371
00:22:17,800 --> 00:22:20,918
The only thing left to do
now is go on the offensive.

372
00:22:22,020 --> 00:22:24,196
Wait, what do you think you're doing?

373
00:22:24,500 --> 00:22:27,457
Running circles around the
building won't do us any good.

374
00:22:27,540 --> 00:22:31,637
If we want to find Robin, then we're
going to have to force our way through.

375
00:22:31,720 --> 00:22:32,550
Huh?

376
00:22:33,180 --> 00:22:35,197
Yeah, but those are just shipwrights.

377
00:22:35,280 --> 00:22:36,677
They're not the bad guys.

378
00:22:36,760 --> 00:22:38,878
Then I'll use the back of my swords.

379
00:22:39,880 --> 00:22:40,710
Huh?

380
00:22:40,793 --> 00:22:43,000
If you want to fight, you get it!

381
00:22:48,380 --> 00:22:50,977
You can still kill people
like that, you know!

382
00:22:51,060 --> 00:22:51,890
No!

383
00:23:10,600 --> 00:23:12,660
Well, what a surprise.

384
00:23:13,320 --> 00:23:16,760
After all this time, I never
thought we'd be meeting here,

385
00:23:17,600 --> 00:23:18,540
Nico Robin.

386
00:23:19,420 --> 00:23:20,949
Am I supposed to know you?

387
00:23:21,540 --> 00:23:23,716
Last night was the first time we met.

388
00:23:24,100 --> 00:23:27,640
But for a long time,
I've wanted to see you.

389
00:23:29,760 --> 00:23:33,525
I even put your wanted poster up
in my room so I'd never forget.

390
00:23:34,120 --> 00:23:36,179
Shall I give you an autograph then?

391
00:23:37,640 --> 00:23:39,740
If you sign it. In blood.

392
00:23:42,260 --> 00:23:44,940
You wanted to kill me? That's right.

393
00:23:45,580 --> 00:23:47,780
Before you destroy the world.

394
00:23:48,960 --> 00:23:51,784
Tell me, why are you
looking for the Poneglyphs?

395
00:23:53,160 --> 00:23:54,700
You must know the risk.

396
00:23:54,860 --> 00:23:56,797
For as long as anyone can remember,

397
00:23:56,880 --> 00:24:00,677
the world government has made it
a serious crime to research them.

398
00:24:00,760 --> 00:24:02,819
Why is that knowledge so important?

399
00:24:04,060 --> 00:24:07,060
If they're so bad, then
why do you know about them?

400
00:24:07,440 --> 00:24:10,499
Knowing that the Poneglyphs
exist is hardly a crime.

401
00:24:10,740 --> 00:24:12,917
But deciphering them is another matter.

402
00:24:13,000 --> 00:24:16,720
And you're the only person in
the world who's capable of that.

403
00:24:17,860 --> 00:24:20,997
That's why the world government put
such a large bounty on your head?

404
00:24:21,080 --> 00:24:23,937
Even though you were only
eight years old at the time.

405
00:24:24,020 --> 00:24:26,677
They fear what you're capable of.

406
00:24:26,760 --> 00:24:28,977
Because you alone have the power.

407
00:24:29,060 --> 00:24:31,340
To revive the ancient weapons.

408
00:24:34,700 --> 00:24:36,560
So, you already know?

409
00:24:39,640 --> 00:24:40,557
Yes, but.

410
00:24:40,640 --> 00:24:44,300
I never would have thought
that CP9 was actually real!

411
00:24:44,980 --> 00:24:46,037
And if that's the case,

412
00:24:46,120 --> 00:24:48,137
that means you've already
left the Straw Hats

413
00:24:48,220 --> 00:24:50,757
and you're helping the
world government now.

414
00:24:50,840 --> 00:24:55,077
A strange choice for a woman who's been
on their most wanted list for 20 years.

415
00:24:55,160 --> 00:24:58,680
But, well, I suppose
that's not my concern.

416
00:24:58,840 --> 00:25:01,877
If you decipher the Poneglyphs
and rebuild one of the weapons,

417
00:25:01,960 --> 00:25:05,297
it doesn't matter if the person
who uses it's good or evil.

418
00:25:05,380 --> 00:25:07,160
It's all the same in the end.

419
00:25:07,540 --> 00:25:10,834
A weapon can never be used
to bring peace to this world.

420
00:25:11,820 --> 00:25:14,460
All it can bring is destruction.

421
00:25:16,060 --> 00:25:18,160
We've buried the evils of the past.

422
00:25:18,420 --> 00:25:20,120
Now let them lie.

423
00:25:23,200 --> 00:25:25,740
You may be right, and I don't disagree.

424
00:25:26,140 --> 00:25:28,380
But you don't know why I'm doing this.

425
00:25:28,600 --> 00:25:32,797
You have no right to tell me what I'm
allowed to do or not do with my research,

426
00:25:32,880 --> 00:25:35,233
or what knowledge I can or cannot learn.

427
00:25:37,220 --> 00:25:39,400
Well, I see what you mean.

428
00:25:40,160 --> 00:25:43,840
But the truth is, we might have
more in common than you think.

429
00:25:44,880 --> 00:25:46,292
Perhaps you didn't know.

430
00:25:46,820 --> 00:25:50,820
But I possess the blueprints for
the ancient weapon known as Pluton.

431
00:25:51,560 --> 00:25:52,900
Then they still exist?

432
00:25:53,640 --> 00:25:58,287
Pluton is the name of a battleship built
on this island many years in the past.

433
00:25:59,940 --> 00:26:02,237
The shipwrights who
created the weapon passed

434
00:26:02,320 --> 00:26:04,677
on the blueprints as a
sort of insurance policy.

435
00:26:04,760 --> 00:26:07,637
They feared that another
battleship of equal power would

436
00:26:07,720 --> 00:26:10,837
be necessary if Pluton ever
fell into the wrong hands.

437
00:26:10,920 --> 00:26:14,657
Thankfully, the ship was lost to
history before that could happen.

438
00:26:14,740 --> 00:26:15,680
And now,

439
00:26:15,860 --> 00:26:18,397
the government wants to
revive that power when

440
00:26:18,480 --> 00:26:21,068
there's no force strong
enough to oppose it.

441
00:26:21,640 --> 00:26:25,717
A part of me hopes that you didn't know
that when you agreed to help them out,

442
00:26:25,800 --> 00:26:27,617
but that really doesn't matter now.

443
00:26:27,700 --> 00:26:31,000
A man named Tom entrusted
those blueprints to me,

444
00:26:31,120 --> 00:26:33,757
and he also told me about
a young girl who was the

445
00:26:33,840 --> 00:26:37,020
sole survivor of the Ohara
incident 20 years ago.

446
00:26:37,320 --> 00:26:39,000
He said despite her age,

447
00:26:39,100 --> 00:26:43,377
she was still dangerous because she had
the same ideology as the devils from Ohara.

448
00:26:43,460 --> 00:26:48,048
In honor of Tom and the other shipwrights,
it's my responsibility to stop you.

449
00:26:48,340 --> 00:26:51,757
Of course, now that the government
knows that the blueprints exist,

450
00:26:51,840 --> 00:26:54,997
the logical solution would be to
burn them and be done with this mess.

451
00:26:55,080 --> 00:26:58,360
But I can't do that because
as long as you're alive,

452
00:26:58,520 --> 00:27:01,520
there's a chance that the
weapon could be refilled.

453
00:27:14,100 --> 00:27:17,080
Is that all you want to
say before you die oh?

454
00:27:18,200 --> 00:27:22,457
And with all due respect, even if you had
killed me, nothing would have changed.

455
00:27:22,540 --> 00:27:26,197
The government doesn't need me
to steal the blueprints from you.

456
00:27:26,280 --> 00:27:29,221
I'm sure they've already
accomplished that anyway.

457
00:27:35,600 --> 00:27:38,480
Well, let's not get
ahead of ourselves here.

458
00:27:41,520 --> 00:27:44,060
You're the ones who've fallen for my trap.

459
00:27:55,620 --> 00:27:57,180
Oh, that's it!

460
00:28:05,180 --> 00:28:07,197
I thought I'd never get out of there.

461
00:28:07,280 --> 00:28:08,633
Man, that was terrible.

462
00:28:08,900 --> 00:28:11,340
Okay, let's get it right this time.

463
00:28:11,540 --> 00:28:13,980
I'll find Robin for sure. Gomp!

464
00:28:15,340 --> 00:28:16,170
Gomp!

465
00:28:18,240 --> 00:28:19,070
Rocket!

466
00:28:37,340 --> 00:28:40,780
I'm afraid you're no match
for our martial arts.

467
00:28:43,480 --> 00:28:48,940
Now stop resisting and hand us the document
before you soil it with your blood.

468
00:28:51,920 --> 00:28:52,837
Damn it.

469
00:28:52,920 --> 00:28:54,777
I really thought.

470
00:28:54,860 --> 00:28:57,060
I could beat him.

471
00:29:05,600 --> 00:29:07,897
I should have known better.

472
00:29:07,980 --> 00:29:10,497
This was all my idea.

473
00:29:10,580 --> 00:29:13,017
Iceberg didn't tell me to fight.

474
00:29:13,100 --> 00:29:16,520
He told me to get the hell out of here.

475
00:29:17,320 --> 00:29:18,457
To run.

476
00:29:18,540 --> 00:29:20,920
and leave the blueprints behind.

477
00:29:23,720 --> 00:29:25,160
You know why?

478
00:29:26,560 --> 00:29:31,020
Because those are nothing
but fakes. What? What?

479
00:29:31,360 --> 00:29:32,880
He can't be serious.

480
00:29:33,200 --> 00:29:34,700
What a waste of time.

481
00:29:35,440 --> 00:29:39,900
I don't know who you are, but this
means your plan's a bust, huh?

482
00:29:40,620 --> 00:29:41,500
Too bad.

483
00:29:41,820 --> 00:29:43,300
Sucks to be you.

484
00:29:43,980 --> 00:29:45,397
The funny thing is,

485
00:29:45,480 --> 00:29:49,715
I don't even know what you bastards
were looking for in the first place.

486
00:29:50,520 --> 00:29:53,760
If you think you've
outwitted CP9, you're wrong.

487
00:29:54,040 --> 00:29:56,275
You're merely delaying the inevitable.

488
00:29:57,520 --> 00:30:00,280
At any rate, even though
you're only a decoy,

489
00:30:00,620 --> 00:30:03,620
now that you know the truth,
we can't let you live.

490
00:30:17,180 --> 00:30:18,020
Damn it!

491
00:30:18,180 --> 00:30:19,560
I got stuck again!

492
00:30:19,840 --> 00:30:21,857
Stupid walls always getting in my way!

493
00:30:21,940 --> 00:30:22,770
I hate them!

494
00:30:22,853 --> 00:30:23,683
I hate them!

495
00:30:23,766 --> 00:30:24,777
Why does this always happen to me?

496
00:30:24,860 --> 00:30:25,690
Straw Hat.

497
00:30:26,320 --> 00:30:27,800
Hey, it's the rope guy!

498
00:30:28,060 --> 00:30:29,640
What's going on in here?

499
00:30:30,200 --> 00:30:31,318
Whoa, are you okay?

500
00:30:31,440 --> 00:30:32,837
You're covered in blood.

501
00:30:32,920 --> 00:30:34,760
You sure did surprise me!

502
00:30:35,080 --> 00:30:36,200
Look who's talking.

503
00:30:36,580 --> 00:30:39,160
At least I'm not crashing through walls.

504
00:30:39,360 --> 00:30:44,080
Straw Hat Luffy, how kind of you to
come here to take blame for the crime.

505
00:30:45,480 --> 00:30:46,640
Oh, I get it!

506
00:30:46,740 --> 00:30:48,437
You guys in the masks
must be the ones that

507
00:30:48,520 --> 00:30:50,597
are forcing Robin to
do all this bad stuff,

508
00:30:50,680 --> 00:30:51,510
huh?

509
00:30:51,593 --> 00:30:52,962
You give her back, you bastards!

510
00:30:53,560 --> 00:30:57,760
If I wasn't stuck right now, you'd
be in big trouble! Tempest kick.

511
00:31:12,040 --> 00:31:13,805
He cut right through the wall!

512
00:31:15,900 --> 00:31:17,380
Hey! Behind you!

513
00:31:28,980 --> 00:31:30,280
What are these?

514
00:31:32,120 --> 00:31:34,280
This is an emergency situation.

515
00:31:34,580 --> 00:31:36,457
We don't have time to deal with you.

516
00:31:36,540 --> 00:31:37,420
I can't move.

517
00:31:37,600 --> 00:31:38,860
Restrain Polly, too.

518
00:31:39,140 --> 00:31:41,237
She's given us enough trouble already.

519
00:31:41,320 --> 00:31:42,150
Right.

520
00:31:57,300 --> 00:31:58,300
It's me.

521
00:31:58,600 --> 00:32:00,306
We've hit a snag in the plan.

522
00:32:00,640 --> 00:32:03,052
Everyone head to the bedroom immediately.

523
00:32:03,460 --> 00:32:05,320
Don't shoot Iceberg yet.

524
00:32:05,760 --> 00:32:06,780
You understand?

525
00:32:06,960 --> 00:32:09,420
I absolutely need him alive.

526
00:32:13,700 --> 00:32:18,057
This has been a delight but I'm
afraid our time is up you see I

527
00:32:18,140 --> 00:32:22,620
have a pressing matter to attend
to running away are you not at all

528
00:32:29,800 --> 00:32:32,240
I'm just finishing you quickly that's all

529
00:32:39,420 --> 00:32:40,420
She's flying!

530
00:32:42,540 --> 00:32:44,220
Hey, you all right?

531
00:32:45,500 --> 00:32:46,540
Are you kidding?

532
00:32:46,860 --> 00:32:48,020
This is nothing.

533
00:32:49,380 --> 00:32:50,680
That's good, I guess.

534
00:32:50,920 --> 00:32:53,449
But why'd you come here
in the first place?

535
00:32:53,580 --> 00:32:57,051
Everyone still thinks you're
the ones who attacked Iceberg.

536
00:32:57,140 --> 00:32:58,846
Sorry about that, by the way.

537
00:32:59,120 --> 00:33:01,557
I realize I might have
jumped the gun a little.

538
00:33:01,640 --> 00:33:02,470
No big deal.

539
00:33:02,680 --> 00:33:04,340
We are pirates, after all.

540
00:33:04,960 --> 00:33:09,195
Anyway, the point is those weird guys
in the masks took one of our crew.

541
00:33:09,520 --> 00:33:11,380
So we're here to get her back.

542
00:33:13,340 --> 00:33:14,300
Nico Robin.

543
00:33:19,800 --> 00:33:22,153
So, you're good at fighting, aren't you?

544
00:33:22,400 --> 00:33:23,280
Hell yeah.

545
00:33:24,020 --> 00:33:26,880
Then you can beat those
guys, huh? You bet.

546
00:33:29,180 --> 00:33:30,010
Good.

547
00:33:30,093 --> 00:33:31,557
We can do this thing together.

548
00:33:31,640 --> 00:33:33,017
Because I'm ready to fight.

549
00:33:33,100 --> 00:33:33,930
Yeah?

550
00:33:34,013 --> 00:33:34,843
Of course I am.

551
00:33:34,926 --> 00:33:38,317
I mean, you think I'm just going to let
some weirdos waltz in out of nowhere,

552
00:33:38,400 --> 00:33:40,459
kick my ass, and then kill Iceberg?

553
00:33:40,640 --> 00:33:41,660
Not a chance!

554
00:33:41,940 --> 00:33:44,137
Who do these punks think they are anyway?

555
00:33:44,220 --> 00:33:46,573
To hell with all this secret agent crap!

556
00:33:49,860 --> 00:33:50,740
Iceberg is...

557
00:33:51,580 --> 00:33:53,400
He's more than just my boss.

558
00:33:53,800 --> 00:33:54,757
He's my teacher.

559
00:33:54,840 --> 00:33:56,252
He made me a shipwright.

560
00:33:56,420 --> 00:33:59,997
I can't let him die! Look
at you. You're a mess.

561
00:34:00,080 --> 00:34:03,277
I told you, I'm ready to fight those
bastards, and I'm not giving up!

562
00:34:03,360 --> 00:34:07,066
I don't care what happens to me,
as long as I can save Iceberg!

563
00:34:08,400 --> 00:34:11,900
Ah, but I can't even move
because I'm stuck to the floor.

564
00:34:12,840 --> 00:34:14,200
This sucks!

565
00:34:14,820 --> 00:34:16,220
Yeah, I know!

566
00:34:16,380 --> 00:34:17,600
This sucks!

567
00:34:18,580 --> 00:34:19,410
Ah!

568
00:34:42,120 --> 00:34:43,220
Go home.

569
00:34:44,860 --> 00:34:47,020
I have nothing to give you people.

570
00:34:47,740 --> 00:34:49,900
Then we have a problem! Don't we?

571
00:34:57,080 --> 00:35:00,240
What does one say to a man
who's marked for death?

572
00:35:02,900 --> 00:35:04,520
First let me be frank.

573
00:35:05,300 --> 00:35:07,080
You disappoint me.

574
00:35:12,600 --> 00:35:13,430
Luchi!

575
00:35:14,260 --> 00:35:15,940
This is your own fault.

576
00:35:19,280 --> 00:35:23,751
You should have handed over the blueprints
when the government asked nicely.

577
00:35:24,420 --> 00:35:25,250
Kaku!

578
00:35:27,020 --> 00:35:27,850
Pity.

579
00:35:27,933 --> 00:35:32,168
I was hoping we could walk away from
this story without resorting to violence.

580
00:35:33,460 --> 00:35:34,290
Kalifa!

581
00:35:34,920 --> 00:35:37,861
It's a shame you're as
hard-headed as your master.

582
00:35:38,400 --> 00:35:39,820
Bruno, from the bar.

583
00:35:40,720 --> 00:35:46,400
That means you've been with
the government all this time.

584
00:35:47,140 --> 00:35:47,970
Indeed.

585
00:35:48,053 --> 00:35:51,380
Needless to say, going undercover
was like second nature to us.

586
00:35:52,500 --> 00:35:57,220
Now, since everyone's being so honest
with each other, let's try this again.

587
00:35:58,780 --> 00:36:01,360
I don't have time to play games.

588
00:36:01,700 --> 00:36:06,077
Tell me, before someone
else gets hurt, where is it?

589
00:36:06,160 --> 00:36:10,620
Where are the blueprints for
the ancient weapon Pluton?
